※ pl4g-test: compile=error diag=4580

※ An ordering is said about one access to one place, so what it is given is the
※ place: a reference and nothing else.  A value has no place to order an access
※ to, and naming a place outright would be a second way of saying what a
※ reference already says.

@[startup, impure]
fn main() → u6:
    let v: u32 = 5u32
    if ⎕acquire(v) = 5u32: 0u6 else: 1u6
